// [fn.type.2] A lambda with no target type that moves out a value it captured is a
// `once fn`: it owns its captures, and calling it uses it up (issue #79). Stage 1 does not
// infer the kind and rejects the move.
// stage1-error: E0502
// expect: hello
// expect: hello again
void Hello() => print("hello");
void Again() => print("hello again");
void Run(once fn() f) { f(); }

fn() h = Hello;
var first = () => {
    fn() g = h;
    g();
};
first();

fn() a = Again;
var second = () => {
    fn() g = a;
    g();
};
Run(second);
